    "answer": "In the implemented Iris protocol slice, restarting ChatRuntime does not preserve conversation context or queued work. According to the Iris protocol v1 slice documentation, \"Restarting ChatRuntime loses context, events, duplicate claims, cancellation state and queued work. Iris history/UUIDs survive but are **not rehydrated into runtime context**.\" The implementation is limited to in-memory persistence, and durable recovery remains future work. Conversation identity is maintained through UUIDs stored in atomic JSON files, but these are not reloaded into the runtime after a restart.",
